     Perhaps you've got an unusal conception of the meaning of "port".
The Unix version is what all the other ports are based on.  The VMS port
is as "official" as any of the others.  Binaries are provided for the
microcomputer versions because of the number of people who wouldn't be
able to build them otherwise.  People on multi-user systems are expected
to build from sources themselves.  VMS binaries happen to be available
at an alternate site.

     If you look at the 'README' file included with the sources, it has a
list of systems where NetHack has been demonstrated or at least reported
to build and run.  The list of Unix variants is vary large...

